{{Short description|Data values of standard electrode potential}}
{{Use American English|date = April 2019}}
{{Main|Standard electrode potential}}

The '''data below''' tabulates [[standard electrode potential]]s (''E''{{su|p={{resize|50%|⦵}}|b=red}}), in [[volt]]s relative to the [[standard hydrogen electrode]] (SHE), at:
* [[Temperature]] {{cvt|298.15|K}};
* [[Activity (chemistry)|Effective concentration]] (activity) {{val|1|u=mol/dm3}} for each [[aqueous solution|aqueous]] or [[Amalgam (chemistry)|amalgamated]] (mercury-alloyed) species;
* Unit [[activity (chemistry)|activity]] for each solvent and pure solid or liquid species; and
* [[Fugacity|Absolute partial pressure]] {{cvt|101.325|kPa|atm bar}} for each gaseous reagent&nbsp;&mdash; the convention in most literature data but not the current [[standard state]] ({{cvt|100|kPa|atm bar}}).
Variations from these ideal conditions affect measured voltage via the [[Nernst equation]].

